Lifecycle Stages 
01. Problem Definition
Define business objectives and key performance indicators (KPIs).

Specify success metrics (e.g., Accuracy, Precision, Recall, RMSE).

02. Data Collection
Gather raw data from databases, APIs, or external static datasets.

Store raw ingestion files securely under data/raw/.

03. Data Cleaning & Preprocessing
Handle missing values, outliers, and data type formatting.

Apply scaling, normalization, and categorical encoding.

04. Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)
Analyze feature distributions, correlations, and target variables.

Generate visual reports and summary statistics inside Jupyter Notebooks.

05. Feature Engineering & Selection
Construct domain-specific derivative features.

Apply variance thresholding, mutual information, or feature importance ranking to isolate key features.

06. Model Selection
Benchmark baseline algorithms (e.g., Logistic Regression, Random Forest, XGBoost).

Choose candidate models based on problem constraints (e.g., inference latency vs. precision).

07. Model Training
Split datasets into training, validation, and test partitions (80/10/10 or 70/15/15).

Train candidate models on training subsets.

08. Model Evaluation and Tuning
Execute cross-validation routines.

Fine-tune hyperparameters via GridSearch, RandomSearch, or Bayesian optimization (Optuna).

09. Model Deployment
Package model artifacts into REST API wrappers (Flask/FastAPI).

Containerize services using Docker for cloud environment deployment (AWS/GCP/Kubernetes).

10. Model Monitoring & Maintenance
Track inference requests, data drift, and model performance metrics over time.

Retrain models automatically when feature distributions shift.
